Refine the 6th color palette only.

Important:
We already have 5 existing light palettes.
Do not remove them.
Do not rename them.
Do not replace the entire design system.
Do not change layouts, flows, navigation structure, breadcrumbs, typography system, tables, cards, filters, drawers, or modals.
Only improve the 6th palette: Dark Mode.

Goal:
The current dark mode feels too loud, too blue, and too intense.
Redesign it so it feels closer to Gmail dark mode:
- soft charcoal background
- neutral dark surfaces
- subtle layered contrast
- muted borders
- light grey text
- restrained blue accents
- clean and calm enterprise feel
- no glowing or neon effect
- no overly saturated navy dashboard look

Design Direction:
Use Gmail dark mode as inspiration, not as a direct copy.
The mood should be:
- quiet
- modern
- highly readable
- low-glare
- professional
- balanced
- neutral
- operational
- refined

Golden Rules:
- Keep the existing 5 color palettes unchanged.
- Keep Dark Mode as the 6th palette.
- Do not redesign the product structure.
- Do not move navigation into page content.
- Follow the established navigation pattern.
- Keep breadcrumbs as they are.
- Keep all existing spacing, hierarchy, component structure, and typography logic.
- Use token-based theming only.
- Do not hardcode dark colors inside components.
- Every component must support the dark tokens.
- Keep the system fully responsive.
- Maintain accessibility and strong readability.
- Avoid harsh visual contrast.
- Avoid pure black large surfaces.
- Avoid neon blue, cyan-glow, or electric accents.
- Avoid overly colorful dark mode.
- Dark mode should feel like Gmail dark mode mixed with an enterprise government system.

Theme Name:
Dark Mode

Updated Gmail-Inspired Dark Palette Tokens:

Core Backgrounds:
- color-bg-app: #202124
- color-bg-sidebar: #171717
- color-bg-topbar: #202124
