How Dark Mode Should Feel:
- app shell: charcoal, not navy
- sidebar: slightly darker than main canvas
- surfaces: subtle elevation through tone difference, not glow
- cards and tables: soft contrast against page background
- selected items: calm filled state
- active states: restrained blue accent
- text: light gray, not pure white everywhere
- borders: visible but subtle
- overall look: closer to Gmail dark, less like a neon analytics dashboard

Apply Dark Mode Across:
- main app shell
- first-level navigation
- second-level navigation
- top bar
- search bar
- year selector
- user profile area
- breadcrumbs
- page titles
- helper text
- cards
- data tables
- table headers
- table rows
- filter bars
- search inputs
- selects
- dropdowns
- buttons
- badges
- pagination
- drawers
- modals
- confirmation dialogs
- tooltip surfaces
- settings / appearance panel
- empty states
- loading states
- custom scrollbars

Navigation Styling in Gmail-Inspired Dark Mode:

First-Level Navigation:
- background: #171717
- inactive icon: #BDC1C6
- inactive text: #BDC1C6
- hover background: #2D2F31
- active item background: #3C4043
- active icon container can use a subtle blue fill or soft highlight
- active icon: #8AB4F8
- active text: #E8EAED
- avoid thick glowing active borders

Second-Level Navigation:
- background: #202124 or #282A2D
- inactive text/icon: #BDC1C6
- hover background: #2D2F31
- active item background: #3C4043
- active text: #E8EAED
- active icon: #8AB4F8
- nested items remain readable and calm
- meaningful icons must stay consistent for all secondary nav items

Top Bar:
- background: #202124
- border-bottom: #3C4043
- search box background: #303134
- search box border: transparent or #3C4043
- search text: #E8EAED
- placeholder: #9AA0A6
- icons: #BDC1C6

Breadcrumbs:
Do not change breadcrumb structure.
Only restyle for dark mode:
- background: transparent
- text: #9AA0A6
- current page: #E8EAED
- separator: #5F6368

Tables in Gmail-Inspired Dark Mode:
Tables must feel like the cleaner direction we want from our design system.
No harsh boxed look.
No loud blue fills.

Table Container:
- background: #282A2D
- border: 1px solid #3C4043
- radius: keep existing system radius
- shadow: subtle only

Table Header:
- background: #303134
- text: #BDC1C6
- bottom border: #3C4043

Table Row:
- default background: #282A2D
- hover background: #2D2F31
- selected background: rgba(138,180,248,0.10)
- row border: #3C4043
- primary text: #E8EAED
- secondary text: #BDC1C6

Table Action Icons:
- default icon: #BDC1C6
- hover icon: #E8EAED
- active icon: #8AB4F8
- action containers should be subtle, not glowing

Status Badges:
Use soft filled badges, not loud saturated pills.

Approved / Success:
- background: rgba(129,201,149,0.14)
- text: #81C995

Pending / Warning:
- background: rgba(251,203,107,0.14)
- text: #FBCB6B

Rejected / Danger:
- background: rgba(242,139,130,0.14)
- text: #F28B82

Info / Under Review:
- background: rgba(138,180,248,0.14)
- text: #8AB4F8

Neutral:
- background: rgba(189,193,198,0.12)
- text: #BDC1C6

Buttons:
Primary:
- background: #8AB4F8
- text: #202124
- hover: #AECBFA
- border: none

Secondary:
- background: #2D2F31
- text: #E8EAED
- border: 1px solid #3C4043
- hover: #3C4043

Ghost:
- background: transparent
- text: #BDC1C6
- hover background: #2D2F31

Danger:
- background: rgba(242,139,130,0.14)
- text: #F28B82
- border: 1px solid rgba(242,139,130,0.22)

Inputs and Filters:
- input background: #303134
- input border: #3C4043
- input text: #E8EAED
- placeholder: #9AA0A6
- focus border: #8AB4F8
- focus ring: rgba(138,180,248,0.28)
- disabled background: #2A2B2E
- disabled text: #80868B

Cards:
- background: #282A2D
- border: 1px solid #3C4043
- title: #E8EAED
- body text: #BDC1C6
- supporting text: #9AA0A6

Modal / Drawer / Panel:
- background: #282A2D
- header background: #282A2D
- footer background: #282A2D
- border: #3C4043
- title: #E8EAED
- body text: #BDC1C6
- overlay: rgba(0,0,0,0.52)

Appearance Panel Rule:
The appearance settings modal/panel should not show random page-specific content like “Report Workspace”.
Keep it generic.
Use neutral preview content only.
For example:
- “Theme Preview”
- “Sample table row”
- “Sample button”
- “Sample input”
- “Sample badge”
Do not inject actual module/page content inside appearance settings.

Scrollbar:
Keep it subtle and theme-aware:
- track: #202124
- thumb: #5F6368
- thumb hover: #8AB4F8

Accessibility:
- Maintain WCAG-friendly contrast where possible
- Do not use low-contrast grey on grey
- Keep focus states visible
- Do not rely only on color for meaning
- Keep all interactions keyboard accessible

Do Not Do:
- do not use bright cyan
- do not use glowing blue borders everywhere
- do not use deep navy as the main app background
- do not use black and electric blue contrast
- do not make cards, tables, or nav look “louder” than Gmail dark mode
- do not add page navigation inside the page body
- do not break the established navigation pattern
- do not change existing 5 palettes

Final Result:
Keep the 5 existing light palettes as they are.
Keep Dark Mode as the 6th palette.
But redesign that 6th palette into a Gmail-inspired dark theme:
charcoal, muted, soft, readable, professional, and calm.